    {
     "id": "c383398",
     "elType": "widget",
     "widgetType": "text-editor",
     "settings": {
      "editor": "<p><strong>Important:</strong> this guide summarises publicly available allergen information to help you plan. It is not medical advice. Schnitz kitchens handle wheat, egg, milk, soy and sesame, so cross-contact is possible. If you have a serious allergy or coeliac disease, speak to the staff and check the official allergen chart before you order.</p><p>The key thing to understand about Schnitz allergens is that the <strong>protein itself (plain chicken) is listed with no allergens</strong>. Most allergens come from the crumb, the breader and the sauces. Choosing a different coating changes what you are eating.</p>"
     },
     "elements": []
    }
   ],
   "isInner": false
