    {
     "id": "e2416a6",
     "elType": "widget",
     "widgetType": "heading",
     "settings": {
      "title": "Is Schnitz Gluten Free?",
      "header_size": "h2"
     },
     "elements": []
    },
    {
     "id": "fda7504",
     "elType": "widget",
     "widgetType": "text-editor",
     "settings": {
      "editor": "<p>Traditional crumbed schnitzels are <strong>not gluten free</strong> &#8211; the flour, egg wash and breadcrumbs all contain gluten. Even the crumb-free lemon pepper flavour is listed as containing gluten. Schnitz does list a gluten free wrap on its allergen chart, but because gluten is everywhere in the kitchen, people with coeliac disease should ask staff how it is prepared before ordering.</p><p>In Australia a product can only be labelled gluten free if it contains no detectable gluten under the Food Standards Code, which is a very high bar for a busy fast food kitchen.</p>"
     },
     "elements": []
    }
   ],
   "isInner": false
